      "card_ids": ["C95", "C101", "C102", "C104", "C117", "C129", "C139", "C141", "C143"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct measured oral bioavailability exists for the query molecule; all evidence is from analogue contexts.",
    "The closest beta-blocker contexts are partly cirrhosis-conditioned, which may overestimate F in a general population; timolol normal-human data mitigate this.",
    "L3 records are AUC and Cmax exposure measurements, not absolute F values, and interaction studies do not define baseline F.",
    "No experimental permeability or first-pass data are available for the urea-containing query; the physicochemical prior is mixed."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is an aryloxypropanolamine beta-blocker analogue with a tert-butylamino side chain and para cyclohexylurea. The closest human contexts, metoprolol, timolol, and propranolol, report oral bioavailability well above 20%, and L3 exposure records confirm measurable human oral absorption for this class. Low values are species- or intervention-specific and do not transfer to the human baseline. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F below 20%. Prediction remains high, confidence moderate, strengthened by L3."
}

